- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `input type="range"` — `min` · `max` · `step` · `value`, and its default actions (keys, pointerdown, click)
  - **How (stack-specific):** Since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, in every document — the browser app's remote pages included — an `input` whose `type` reads `range` (ASCII case-insensitive) holds a current value apart from its `value` attribute (`RangeInputData`, an `f64`), and the markup and the user's keys and pointer move it within bounds: the four attributes are read through `parse_float`, the HTML rules for parsing floating-point number values, a parse error, NaN or an infinity reading as absent and `-0` as `0` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:232-270; its private steps `take_sign`, `take_digits` and `take_exponent` since 2026-10-16-handler-splits-and-readme, the readings unchanged, packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:272-301); `min` defaults to 0 and `max` to 100, a `max` below `min` reading as `min`; `step` defaults to 1, a step ≤ 0 or unparsable reading 1 and `any` setting no grid and stepping by 1 on a key; the step base is `min` where it parses, else the `value` attribute, else 0; the default value is the midpoint, computed `min/2 + max/2` so it cannot overflow; every seed, attribute write and move is sanitized — clamped to `[min, max]`, moved to the nearest grid value, the greater on a tie, the grid index computed `value/step − base/step` so the difference of two finite bounds cannot overflow, then rounded to the decimals of the step and the base and written in its shortest round-trip form (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:67-75; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:85-206) — so the value stays finite, bounded and on its grid on degenerate markup (an 8-row unit table, packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:471-507, and 7 integration rows in both layout modes, tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:181-222);
 the default actions: on a focused range input with no `disabled` attribute (presence) a pressed `ArrowRight` or `ArrowUp` steps up, `ArrowLeft` or `ArrowDown` steps down, `Home` and `End` go to the minimum and the maximum, and every other key does nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:106-111; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:156-173); a main-button pointerdown, its arm after the `disabled` arm, sets the value from the hit's fraction of the content box, clamped to `[0, 1]`, a content box of no width reading 0 (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:462-466; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:725-736; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:522-524; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:738-753); a click, after the `disabled` check, focuses it and changes no value (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:840-852); every change goes through one path that marks the changed set and fires one `input` event carrying the formatted value, a move that changes nothing firing none (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:532-553); a disabled range takes neither key nor click (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:240-262); a `value` write re-seeds the current value and a `min`, `max` or `step` write or removal re-sanitizes it — a departure from the spec's dirty-value flag, the cost the founder's first fork answer took on (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:349-355; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:380-382; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:515-522); the rules module holds no print, log site, `unwrap`, `expect`, panic or env read outside its tests, and the chunk's added engine lines none either (the gate censuses read 0);
 the current value leaves only as form submission's entry (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:330-331), the `input` event's value and the snapshot's `NodeState.value` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:263-265) — a control value, crossing the driver's answers and MCP results inside the ratified carriers, with no carrier, verb, field, log field or span added — and no accessibility node value or action changes — an engine change for every document and a boundary widening, ratified by the founder: his ruling of 2026-10-07 «Пусть будет а», his answers to the three forks of 2026-10-13 «Отдельное текущее значение», «Стрелки + Home/End (Рекомендую)» and «Клик даёт фокус (Рекомендую)», and his confirm of the wrap's answer card the same day «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)», which also covers the three consequences the operator confirmed at the review — each by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label, the English wording the overseer's — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-range-input-interaction/report.md

- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `select` (single-choice) — its choice, keys and typeahead, click, the `selected` attribute, an option's `label` · `value`, the `change` event
  - **How (stack-specific):** In every document, remote pages included: a `select` without `multiple` holds its choice as its options' `CHECKED` state, seeded from a `selected` attribute at creation, a `selected` write exclusive and a cleared one unchosen, every recorded select settled at the mutator's flush and on entering the document by HTML's selectedness setting algorithm — the last chosen, else the first option not disabled; a `multiple` write or removal records the select, so removal settles it to one, and `set_option_selectedness` leaves a `multiple` select's other options alone (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1334-1343; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:472-478; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1113-1116; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1206-1210; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1345-1367; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:258-267); its rules, cited to the WHATWG `select` element, read the select's `option` children and those of its `optgroup` children, in tree order (the `optgroup` row), an option's label (its non-empty `label` attribute, else its stripped and collapsed text) and its value (its `value` attribute, else the text) (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:18-304); on a focused single-choice select that `ElementData::is_disabled` does not read disabled, its list closed, a pressed `ArrowDown` / `ArrowUp` takes the next / previous enabled option, `Home` / `End` the first / last, a `Key::Character` with no Ctrl, Alt or Meta is typeahead, Enter opens its list, a Space with no typed text standing opens it (`press_select_key`) and every other key does nothing — a closed key match (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:112-117; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:171-255); typeahead keeps the typed text in the document's private `select_typeahead` buffer, starting afresh for another select or after 1 s of the document's clock, and chooses the first enabled option whose label starts with it, compared in lower case, an empty text matching nothing — compared, never kept past 1 s and never carried out (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:375-396; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:294-304);
 a click on a select, past `handle_click`'s `is_disabled` walk gate, clears the typeahead and the text selection and focuses it, and on a single select opens its list or closes one standing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:947-960); every choice goes through one path that marks the changed set and dispatches `input` then the engine-emitted `change` (not cancelable, bubbling), each carrying `BaseDocument::select_value`, a choice of the chosen option firing nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:470-496; packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:150; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:397-402); the choice leaves only as form submission's entries (every chosen option not disabled, packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:276-286), the `input` and `change` events' value, the snapshot's `value` (the chosen option's value, no mask applying) and the options' tree nodes — an option under a select kept in the accessibility tree though it computes `display: none`, its `selected` written from its state, its `label` attribute its name (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:164-170; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:184-194; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:284-285; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:245-269) — inside the ratified name and control-value crossings; the driver's `type` on a single select is the same typeahead, reached through `focus_select` with no click, so it fires no DOM focus events and leaves no list open, a text opening on a space typing nothing there (a `multiple` select's, its own row below), its help fixed text (packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:240-243); no print, log site, env read or panic path in the rules module, and no carrier, verb, argument, key name, result field, cause, session error, exit, log field or span added; stated limits: an option of a closed single select has no click arm and stays refused `covered`, under a group too, and a single select's `size` is not read; pinned by the rules module's 8 unit tests, `select_interaction` 18 and `stand_act_select` 10, both layout modes, as measured at escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-10-31-engine-debts/report.md (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_interaction.rs:125-356;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_select.rs:85-270) — an engine change for every document and a boundary widening, ratified — as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-20-select-by-id/report.md, the list's keys, click and `type` at escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-10-31-select-popup/report.md
